.TH ESDM\-ES\-EXT\-SERVE 8 "2026-10-16" "ESDM @VERSION@" "ESDM Manual"
.SH NAME
esdm\-es\-ext\-serve \- serve an external entropy source plugin to the ESDM
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B esdm\-es\-ext\-serve
.B \-\-plugin
.I LIBRARY
.B \-\-socket
.I PATH
.RB [ \-\-mode
.IR MODE ]
.RB [ \-\-client_uid
.IR USER ]...
.RB [ \-v ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B esdm\-es\-ext\-serve
loads the external entropy source plugin library
.I LIBRARY
\- see
.BR libesdm_es_ext (3)
\- and serves it on the UNIX domain socket
.IR PATH ,
which
.B esdm\-server \-\-es_ext_socket
.I PATH
connects to. The plugin that
.B esdm\-server \-\-es_ext_lib
would load into the daemon runs in a process of its own this way: with its
own privileges, in its own address space, and restarted on its own.
.PP
The plugin is loaded and initialized before the socket is served; a plugin
library that cannot be loaded, exports no plugin of the supported version or
fails its initialization ends the program with exit status 1. It serves until
it receives
.BR SIGTERM ,
.B SIGINT
or
.BR SIGHUP ,
then removes the socket and exits with status 0.
.PP
The ESDM accepts a provider running as root, or as the user given with
.BR "esdm\-server \-\-es_ext_socket_uid" .
It connects with its privileges dropped once a connection was lost, so the
socket has to let the user the ESDM runs as connect \- by default
.BR nobody ,
hence the default mode 0666. A more restrictive mode needs the ESDM to run with
a group that is granted access
.RB ( "esdm\-server \-\-groupname" ).
.PP
In turn, only clients running as root or as a user given with
.B \-\-client_uid
are served \- by default root and
.BR nobody ,
the user the ESDM runs as unless told otherwise. Any other client is
disconnected at once, so that it can neither take the few client slots the
ESDM needs nor drain the noise source.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-plugin " \fILIBRARY\fR"
Plugin library of the entropy source.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-socket " \fIPATH\fR"
Socket to serve it on. A socket left at the path by an earlier instance is
replaced, any other file is not.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mode " \fIMODE\fR"
Access mode of the socket, octal. The default is 0666.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-client_uid " \fIUSER\fR"
Serve clients running as
.I USER
\- a uid or a user name \- next to root. May be given up to 8 times; the
default is
.BR nobody .
Give the user of
.B esdm\-server \-\-username
if the ESDM runs as another one.
.TP
.B \-\-no_dtls
Do not offer DTLS to the clients. A build with DTLS (meson option
.BR dtls )
offers it by default, see
.BR libesdm_es_ext (3).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Verbose logging; repeat for more.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
esdm\-es\-ext\-serve \-\-plugin /usr/lib/esdm/my_es.so \\
	\-\-socket /run/esdm\-es\-ext.socket
esdm\-server \-\-es_ext_socket /run/esdm\-es\-ext.socket
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libesdm_es_ext (3),
.BR esdm\-server (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Markus Theil <theil.markus@gmail.com>
